PART 2 — COMPLETE ROLE-BASED AUTHENTICATION
==================================================

Extend the existing authentication system to support:

- Student
- Parent
- Teacher
- Admin

Every authenticated user must have a server-verified role.

LOGIN FLOW:

1. User enters credentials.
2. Backend authenticates the user.
3. Backend retrieves the user's authorized role and account status.
4. Backend validates whether the account is active.
5. User is redirected to the appropriate dashboard.

Teacher accounts must access the Teacher Dashboard.

Student accounts must access the Student Dashboard.

Parent accounts must access the Parent Dashboard.

Admin accounts must access the Admin Dashboard.

IMPORTANT SECURITY RULES:

- Never trust a role supplied by the frontend.
- Never allow users to change their own role.
- Never authorize access based only on a hidden button or frontend route.
- Enforce authorization on every protected backend endpoint.
- Reject unauthorized API requests even if a user manually changes request parameters.
- Do not expose administrative endpoints to teachers or students.
- A teacher must not be able to become an Admin by editing a request.

Only Admin can create, approve, deactivate, or modify teacher accounts and permissions.

